c. acts of neglecting persons within the scope of the household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or by reason of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to such persons; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by limiting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of such person.

