a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.
(3) In carrying out the duties and functions as referred to in paragraph (2), the regional government cooperates with government agencies, provincial governments, other regency/city governments, communities, families and parents.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for services and handling of women and child victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 7

Neglect as referred to in Article 3 letter d is caused by:

a. acts that result in the non-fulfillment of the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after children as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of neglecting persons within the scope of the household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or by reason of an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to such persons; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by limiting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of such person.

